hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2859","Narrated Sa'eed bin Hilal:that Jabir bin 'Abdullah Al-Ansari said: ""One day the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to us and said: ""While I was sleeping I had a vision as if Jibra'il was at my feet. One of them said to his companion: 'Make a parable for him' so he said: 'Listen so that your ears may hear. Hearken so that your heart may understand! The parable of you and your Ummah is but the parable of a king who conquers a land"
"2860","Narrated Abu 'Uthman An-Nahdi:from Ibn Mas'ud who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed 'Isha"
"2861","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The parable of myself and the Prophets [before myself] is that of a man who constructed a house. He completed it and made it well"
"2862","Narrated Al-Harith Al-Ash'ari:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah commanded Yahya bin Zakariyya with five commandments to abide by"
"2863","# Hadith Translation

**Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshār, narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, from Thābit ibn ʿImāra al-Ḥanafī, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:**

**""Every eye is adulterous (zāniyah), and when a woman applies perfume and passes by a gathering, she is such and such"" — meaning, an adulteress (zāniyah).**

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** There are narrations on this topic from Abū Hurayrah. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ (good and authentic) hadith.

---

*Note: This hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and addresses the broader Islamic principle of modesty and the avoidance of fitnah (temptation), emphasizing that the gaze itself is a form of zinā (adultery) of the eyes, as established in other well-known narrations, and that a woman going out with conspicuous perfume carries a similar moral weight in terms of the potential for temptation.*"
"2864","that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Fragrance for men is that which its scent is apparent and its color is hidden, and fragrance for women is that which its color is visible and its scent is hidden."" (Meaning when leaving the home as indicated by the previous chapter. As far as in the presence of the husband, then the woman may wear fragrant perfume.)"
"2865","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The parable of the believer is like the plant; the wind does not stop causing it to sway"
"2866","""The Prophet (ﷺ) said : 'Indeed the best fragrance for men is what's scent is apparent and its color is hidden, and the best fragrance for women is what's color is visible and its scent is hidden.' And he prohibited Mitharatil-Urjawan (Mitharah was some type of saddle cloth. Some of the people of knowledge say it was a certain kind of cloth made of silk, and it preceded earlier under no. 1760. They disagree over Al-Urjawan, and perhaps it means whatever is red, meaning the Red Mitahrah, see Tuhfat Al-Ahwadhi)."""
"2867","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do you think that if there was a river by the gate of one of you"
"2868","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The parable of my Ummah is that of a rain; it is not known if its beginning is better or its end"
"2869","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Buraidah:from his father that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Do you know what the parable of this and this is?"" - and he tossed two pebbles. They said: ""Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) know better."" He said: ""This (the farther) one is hope"
"2870","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Your period in comparison to the periods of the previous nations"
"2871","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'A man is not to look at the 'Awrah of a man, and a woman is not to look at the 'Awrah of a woman. A man is not to be alone with a man under one garment, and a woman is not to be alone with a woman under one garment.'"""
"2872","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:**

""I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, what of our private parts should we conceal and what may we expose?' He ﷺ said: **'Guard your private parts, except from your wife or those whom your right hand possesses (i.e., female captives/slaves).'**

I said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, if people are in close proximity to one another?' He ﷺ said: **'If you are able to ensure that no one sees it, then let no one see it.'**

I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, if one of us is alone?' He ﷺ said: **'Then Allah is more deserving that one should feel modesty before Him.'**

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: *This is a hasan (good) hadith.*""

---

**Source:** Sunan al-Tirmidhi

**Grading:** Hasan (Good) — as graded by Imam Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi"
"2873","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Parable of myself and that of my Ummah is that of a man who kindled a fire"
"2874","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to Ubayy bin Ka'b"
